1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,516
The Strait Stays Closed

2
00:00:03,516 --> 00:00:28,976
On March 12 the first statement of the new Supreme Leader, Mojtaba Khamenei, aired on state television. There was no voice of his own. An announcer read it for him. The statement said the Strait of Hormuz would stay closed and warned countries hosting U.S. bases. The same day the U.N. refugee agency said the war had driven three million people from their homes inside Iran.

3
00:00:29,576 --> 00:00:58,108
The same day fire broke out in the laundry spaces of the carrier USS Gerald R. Ford in the Red Sea. Two sailors were hurt and more than 600 lost their bunks. Fighting it and cleaning up took thirty hours. In western Iraq a U.S. Air Force KC-135 tanker crashed, killing all six crew. Ten Iranian multiple-warhead missiles fell on Tel Aviv, injuring 124.

4
00:00:58,708 --> 00:01:22,728
On March 13 U.S. forces bombed Kharg Island, the hub of Iran’s crude exports. President Trump said every military facility on the island had been destroyed. In Tehran an explosion during the Quds Day march killed one person. The State Department posted rewards of up to $10 million on ten Iranian leaders, Mojtaba Khamenei among them.

5
00:01:23,328 --> 00:01:27,116
Epic Fury continues in Episode 6.
